{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Vizing's theorem: every finite simple graph G has a proper edge colouring with Δ(G) + 1 colours, stated with Mathlib's line graph (G.lineGraph is (Δ(G) + 1)-colourable, hence χ'(G) ≤ Δ(G) + 1), proved with fans and Kempe chain exchanges. It also proves the equitable refinement: for every c ≥ Δ(G) + 1 there is a proper edge colouring with colours Fin c in which any two colour classes (including unused colours) differ in size by at most one (McDiarmid 1972), obtained by balancing a Vizing colouring with alternating-component moves that strictly decrease a square energy. Version 2 adds the lower bound Δ(G) ≤ χ'(G) (the edges at a vertex of maximum degree form a clique of the line graph) and hence the dichotomy χ'(G) ∈ {Δ(G), Δ(G) + 1} (class 1 / class 2).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
    }
  ],
